      "raw": "[quote=\"Bunston\"]\n<b>Ironic wrote:</b>\n<div class=\"bb-quote\"><blockquote class=\"bb-quote-body\">Well, if Peter says that, it must be so.</blockquote></div>\nI feel like this is a very dangerous line of thinking.\n[/quote]\nAw, what&#39;s the craziest thing that might come up?\n[quote=\"PeterCHayward\"]\n\nCon, of Con&#39;s Bunker, is obviously the lovechild of Bunker and Guise. Bunker because he named his house after his father, of course, and Guise - and here&#39;s the part that I&#39;m less sure of - because of Guise&#39;s card &quot;Ret Con&quot;.\n\nRet, as we all know, is short for Reticulate, which could either be a reference to a Reticulated Python OR - and this is the thought that makes the most sense to me - Reticulating Splines, the infamous loading screen from the Sims 1, 2, and 3.\n\nThere were 3 Sims games, just like the original game came with 3 flesh-and-blood villains. But wait! The original game came with four villains, only one of whom was a robot. A robot like they had in <em>The Jetsons</em> - not exactly the same, but if you look carefully at some of the background Sentinels art I&#39;m sure you&#39;ll see it backs up what I&#39;m saying.\n\nNow The Jetsons was set in the future - the same future that Con lives in? I&#39;m not sure, but all evidence points to yes. The four members of the Jetson family - George, Jane, Judy and Elroy - have all the vowels in their names <strong>except</strong> &quot;i&quot;. You&#39;ll see why this is significant in a second.\n\nThe dog was called &quot;Astro&quot;, which I think we can agree explains why Wagner Mars base has a METEOR storm instead of an ASTEROID storm - if it was an Asteroid Storm, people would think that Astro was incapable of causing damage, whereas my theory relies on him turning out to be a Scion for OblivAeon all along (if you could confirm that while we&#39;re here that would be great).\n\nSo OblivAeon has all the vowels except &quot;U&quot; and the Jetsons have all the vowels except &quot;I&quot;, and - and here&#39;s the bit where shit really gets real - &quot;Con&quot;, &quot;Bunker&quot;, and &quot;Guise&quot; have ALL the vowels between them.\n\nI&#39;m sure you can see where I&#39;m going with this.\n\nSo Christopher, my big question, arguably the most important question you&#39;re going to be asked in this whole AMA - when Guise/Bunker (my personal fan-name for them is &quot;Buise&quot;, but I&#39;m not one of those people who really hate the &quot;Gunker&quot; camp) gave birth to Con, which one of them was pregnant? Guise or Bunker?\n[/quote]\nSee?&nbsp; IT ALL MAKES SENSE.\n",
