      "created_at": "2016-03-10T18:00:28.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Well, apart from the fact that \"Reticulating Splines\" pre-dates The Sims by at least a few years as I associate it with Sim City 2000 (which is older, though I don't recall by how much - I don't know if it came out <em>in</em> 2000 or before then) and the fact that \"Con\", \"Bunker\", and \"Guise\" only contain all the vowels if the letter A is declared no longer a vowel, yep, sure that entire theory makes complete sense, yup, definitely ;).</p>",
